{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986003-contested-actions-and-resistance","id":986003,"title":"Contested Actions and Resistance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T01:39:16-07:00","id":986003,"title":"Contested Actions and Resistance","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm preparing for my first Chronicle, and I have a couple of questions about rolling dice:<br /> <br /> 1) In the case of a contested action, who wins in the event of a tie?<br /> 2) On pg 171 of VtR 2nd ed. there is a paragraph on Resistance. It says &quot;Resistance applies in situations where the number of successes on the roll is an important factor&quot;. Then, in the next paragraph, it talks about the Argument action, which is Intelligence + Expression - victim's Resolve. I'm confused because the results are listed as Dramatic Failure, Failure, Success, Exceptional Success. In other words, the number of successes doesn't seem to matter (unless you get 5+). Can someone explain this to me?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T01:55:40-07:00","id":986008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LogicalUnit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986003-contested-actions-and-resistance#post986003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) In the case of a contested action, who wins in the event of a tie?</div> </div> </div> </div>This largely depends on the context of the action - often, ties will work out in the defender's favor because the aggressor not making any meaningful progress is functionally the same result as failing. But, in some cases, you might need to determine a definitive winner and loser in the contest. In this case, I would recommend simply rolling again until someone achieves more successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LogicalUnit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986003-contested-actions-and-resistance#post986003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) On pg 171 of VtR 2nd ed. there is a paragraph on Resistance. It says &amp;quot;Resistance applies in situations where the number of successes on the roll is an important factor&amp;quot;. Then, in the next paragraph, it talks about the Argument action, which is Intelligence + Expression - victim's Resolve. I'm confused because the results are listed as Dramatic Failure, Failure, Success, Exceptional Success. In other words, the number of successes doesn't seem to matter (unless you get 5+). Can someone explain this to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>The guideline to use resistance when the number of successes matters and contested actions when it doesn't is pretty rough, and isn't always used by the book. I think in the case of the sample actions, they were using resistance when defending against the action is passive, and contested actions when it's something you have to actively try to resist. I'm kind of surprised that wasn't the suggested guideline, because it seems like that's more often how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T02:14:45-07:00","id":986009,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks for the explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4824-logicalunit","name":"LogicalUnit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}